rd on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September and September to October each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 54% of normal in January to February and 57% in September to October. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 184% of normal and June to July at 132% on the middle of the grids. June to July is the wettest pair at 8.52 inches and January to February the driest at 3.15.</p>"}
